{
  "title": "torch.profiler.profile cannot save trace",
  "issue_id": "167707",
  "bug_description": "Repro:\n```python\nimport torch\n\nworker_name = \"trace\"\nprofile = torch.profiler.profile(\n        activities=[\n            torch.profiler.ProfilerActivity.CPU,\n            torch.profiler.ProfilerActivity.CUDA,\n        ],\n        on_trace_ready=torch.profiler.tensorboard_trace_handler(\n            \".\", worker_name=worker_name, use_gzip=True\n        ),\n    )\n\n\nprofile.start()\n\nx = torch.randn(2, device=\"cuda\")\ny = x + 21\nz = x * 15\nprofile.stop()\n```\n\nOn Pytorch main branch (d105e3a198ec40865692fc1f72b9e95b324f97ab, Nov 12), the saved trace is broken.\nOn PyTorch 2.8.0, the saved trace can be viewed correctly.\nOn PyTorch 2.9.1, the saved trace can be viewed correctly.\n\nThis breaks [vllm profiler](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/blob/main/vllm/v1/worker/gpu_worker.py#L108-L120).\n\n\ncc @chauhang @penguinwu @zou3519 @huydhn",
